LaTeX output requires you to include the following LaTeX commands:

**Formatting your output:**

```latex
\documentclass{standalone}
\begin{document}
\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{photon_energy_spectrum}
\caption{Energy distribution of photons in a semiconductor}
\end{figure}
\end{document}
```

**Adding the formatted figures:**

```latex
\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{photon_energy_spectrum}
\caption{Energy distribution of photons in a semiconductor}
\label{fig:photon_energy_spectrum}
\end{figure}
```

**Important notes:**
1. The `\includegraphics` command requires the actual image file path
2. For better readability, label the image appropriately in your figure caption
3. If your section includes multiple figures, use the `figure` environment instead of repeating the `\includegraphics` commands
4. Always double-check your figure caption text for typos
5. Use `\begin{figure}[h]` and `\end{figure}` for consistent formatting

